"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[20967],{520967:e=>{e.exports="# Temporary Tables & CTEs\n\nSource dialect temp table patterns → Delta temporary views, CTEs, and staging tables.\n\n> For DBSQL temporary table syntax, load `skills/writing-sql/temp-table.md`.\n\n## MSSQL\n\n### Temporary tables\n\n**Critical limitations of DBSQL TEMP TABLE:**\n\n1. **SQL warehouse sessions only** — Not supported in Notebook or Jobs contexts running on classic or serverless compute clusters; only available inside a SQL warehouse session\n2. **No `ALTER TABLE`** — Cannot add/drop columns after creation\n3. **Session-scoped** — Dropped automatically when the session ends\n\n```sql\n-- T-SQL\nSELECT * INTO #staging FROM source WHERE condition;\n\n-- DBSQL\nCREATE TEMP TABLE staging_data AS SELECT * FROM source WHERE condition;\n```\n\n**Preferred alternatives:**\n\n```sql\n-- CTEs (best for single-query scope)\nWITH temp_data AS (SELECT * FROM source WHERE condition)\nSELECT * FROM temp_data;\n\n-- Temporary views (session-scoped, works on serverless)\nCREATE OR REPLACE TEMPORARY VIEW temp_data AS SELECT * FROM source WHERE condition;\n\n-- Permanent staging tables in Unity Catalog (most flexible for multi-step ETL)\nCREATE TABLE my_catalog.staging.temp_data AS SELECT ...;\n-- ... use ...\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS my_catalog.staging.temp_data;\n```\n\n### SELECT INTO #temp\n\n```sql\n-- T-SQL\nSELECT customer_id, SUM(amount) AS total\nINTO #customer_totals\nFROM orders\nGROUP BY customer_id;\n\n-- DBSQL (temp view approach)\nCREATE OR REPLACE TEMPORARY VIEW customer_totals AS\nSELECT customer_id, SUM(amount) AS total\nFROM orders\nGROUP BY customer_id;\n```\n\n### Global temporary tables (##temp)\n\nT-SQL `##GlobalTemp` (cross-session visible) has no direct DBSQL equivalent. Use a permanent staging table with a unique name in Unity Catalog and DROP it after use.\n\n**Naming strategy to avoid collisions under concurrent pipeline runs**: include a run identifier in the table name so parallel executions don't clobber each other.\n\n```sql\n-- Naming pattern: include a run_id or timestamp suffix\n-- In a Databricks Workflow, use the job run ID: {{ job.run_id }} (available as a task parameter)\n\n-- Create with unique name\nCREATE TABLE my_catalog.staging.global_temp_orders_run_12345 AS\nSELECT * FROM source WHERE condition;\n\n-- ... use across multiple sessions/tasks ...\n\n-- Drop when done\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS my_catalog.staging.global_temp_orders_run_12345;\n```\n\nIf a run ID is not available, use a UUID generated before the pipeline starts and passed as a parameter to all tasks that share the staging table.\n\n### Table variables (@variable TABLE)\n\nT-SQL table variables have no DBSQL equivalent. The right replacement depends on usage scope:\n\n**Single-query scope** (the table variable is only referenced inside one SELECT): replace with a CTE.\n\n```sql\n-- T-SQL\nDECLARE @t TABLE (id INT, val VARCHAR(50));\nINSERT INTO @t SELECT id, val FROM source;\nSELECT * FROM @t;\n\n-- DBSQL (single-query)\nWITH t AS (SELECT id, val FROM source)\nSELECT * FROM t;\n```\n\n**Multi-statement scope** (the table variable is populated once and queried across several separate statements): replace with a temporary view. A CTE does not work here because it is only visible inside the single statement that defines it.\n\n```sql\n-- T-SQL multi-statement pattern\nDECLARE @t TABLE (id INT, val VARCHAR(50));\nINSERT INTO @t SELECT id, val FROM source WHERE active = 1;\nUPDATE other SET flag = 1 WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM @t);\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM @t;\n\n-- DBSQL: temp view (session-scoped, visible across multiple statements)\nCREATE OR REPLACE TEMPORARY VIEW t AS SELECT id, val FROM source WHERE active = 1;\nUPDATE other SET flag = 1 WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM t);\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM t;\n```\n\n### Table-Valued Parameters (TVPs)\n\nNo DBSQL equivalent. Replace with:\n\n- Temporary staging table populated before the call\n- Serialized array parameter passed as JSON string\n\n## SYNAPSE\n\nSame as MSSQL. Additionally, Synapse CTAS with distribution hints:\n\n```sql\n-- Synapse CTAS\nCREATE TABLE #distributed_temp WITH (DISTRIBUTION = HASH(id)) AS SELECT ...;\n\n-- DBSQL (distribution is automatic; no hint needed)\nCREATE TEMP TABLE distributed_temp AS SELECT ...;\n```\n"}}]);
